## Context

During the 2026-07-14 seat audits (0207 log), `z-ai/glm-5.2` and
`moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code` never completed a review: the reviewer process
inside the sandbox produced NO stderr and idled until SEAT_TIMEOUT killed
it (reproduced at 300s and 540s caps; terra completes the same diff in
~30s). A direct API probe exonerates the models: both answer a trivial
prompt over the same endpoint and key in 1-3s, HTTP 200, finish=stop —
and both return a `reasoning` field alongside `content`. Models that
worked (gpt-5.6-terra/luna, gpt-4o-mini, deepseek-v4-flash,
qwen3-coder-next) either emit no reasoning field or a shape the stack
tolerates. Hypothesis: the seat's pinned aider/litellm venv mishandles
reasoning-model responses via the `openai/` route — hangs waiting for
content it never surfaces.

This blocks auditioning reasoning-emitting candidates — half the
OpenRouter leaderboard 0346's audition board wants to scan.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/seat-runner.sh` — SEAT_TIMEOUT kill is the only symptom surface
- the aider uv-tool venv (allowlisted into the sandbox) — pinned litellm
  version lives there
- `tickets/0346-reviewers-audition-retrospective-benchm.erg` — consumer

## Actions

1. Reproduce outside the sandbox: aider --ask against OpenRouter
   glm-5.2 via the openai/ route; capture where it hangs (litellm
   streaming? response parse?).
2. Fix smallest-first: litellm/aider upgrade, or a per-model extra-body
   param suppressing the reasoning field, or a response-shim in the seat.
3. Canary: a cheap seat self-test invocation against a reasoning-model
   stub so the incompatibility class is caught before an audition burns
   wall-clock.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] glm-5.2 and kimi-k2.7-code complete a seat review (or the stack
      fails LOUD with a diagnostic, not a silent timeout)
- [ ] Canary test pins the reasoning-response shape
- [ ] `make check` passes
